## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to integrate simple ICA with audio-visual cues under practical latency constraints, mirroring real-world video conferencing scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- **Online ICA**: Processing two-channel audio in a streaming fashion using STFT
- **Cross-modal permutation alignment**: Using lip movement as a visual cue to resolve frequency-wise permutation ambiguity
- **Feature extraction**: Lip kinematics (lip width, height, aperture) from video; spectral envelopes from audio
- **Latency considerations**: Target end-to-end latency under 100ms for real-time performance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lip-audio alignment score computation
function computeLipAudioScore(lipKinematics, audioEnvelope) {
  const normalizedLip = normalize(lipKinematics);
  const normalizedAudio = normalize(audioEnvelope);
  return correlation(normalizedLip, normalizedAudio);
}

// Permutation resolution using visual cues
function resolvePermutation(icaOutputs, lipScores) {
  // Assign frequency bins to sources based on highest lip correlation
  return assignFrequencyBins(icaOutputs, lipScores);
}
```

